  <file path="/home/efeins/.codex/worktrees/marmorstein-projects/master/project/prayerbook_for_the_new_year-heidenheim-1965-he/index.xml"><tei:note xmlns:tei="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" type="description" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n167.jpg" xml:lang="en">Before reading from the Torah, the individual called upon says the following:</tei:note>
        <tei:note xmlns:tei="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" type="instruction" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n167.jpg" xml:lang="en">He then repeats this and continues:</tei:note>
        <tei:note xmlns:tei="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" type="instruction" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n167.jpg" xml:lang="en">Then the reading of the Torah begins until the end of the portion when the individual who had been called upon, says:</tei:note>
        <tei:note xmlns:tei="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" type="instruction" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n189.jpg" xml:lang="en">On Sabbath the following prayer is recited before <tei:foreign xml:lang="he">אשרי</tei:foreign></tei:note>
        </file>
