  <file path="/home/efeins/.codex/worktrees/marmorstein-projects/master/project/prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en/index.xml"><tei:note xmlns:tei="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" type="instruction" xml:lang="en">On Sabbath we say <tei:foreign xml:lang="he">שמו מפארים</tei:foreign> etc., as below.</tei:note>
            <tei:note xmlns:tei="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" type="description" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n168.jpg" xml:lang="en">Before reading from the Torah, the individual called upon says the following:</tei:note>
        <tei:note xmlns:tei="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" type="instruction" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n168.jpg" xml:lang="en">He then repeats this and continues:</tei:note>
        <tei:note xmlns:tei="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" type="instruction" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n168.jpg" xml:lang="en">Then the reading of the Torah begins until the end of the portion when the individual who had been called upon, says:</tei:note>
        <tei:note xmlns:tei="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" type="instruction" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n172.jpg" xml:lang="en">The second scroll of the Torah is then placed next to the first on the reading desk and the Reader says half-kaddish. The first scroll is then raised and rolled together. After that, the second scroll is unrolled and someone is called to the reading for Maphtir which is taken from Pinhas.</tei:note>
        <tei:note xmlns:tei="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" type="instruction" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n174.jpg" xml:lang="en">After the reading, the Torah scroll is lifted up and rolled together again. When the Torah scroll is being lifted up, one says:</tei:note>
        <tei:note xmlns:tei="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" type="instruction" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n174.jpg" xml:lang="en">Blessing before the Haphtorah:</tei:note>
        <tei:note xmlns:tei="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" type="instruction" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n182.jpg" xml:lang="en">Blessings after the Haphtorah:</tei:note>
        <tei:note xmlns:tei="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" type="instruction" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n190.jpg" xml:lang="en">On Sabbath the following prayer is recited before <tei:foreign xml:lang="he">אשרי</tei:foreign></tei:note>
        </file>
